{#- Root layout. All document metadata (charset, viewport, title, canonical,
     robots, theme-color, favicons, manifest, feeds, Open Graph, JSON-LD)
     comes from partials/head.njk (P1.9, owned by seo-specialist) — this
     layout must not duplicate any of it. base.njk contributes only the
     structural shell: html lang, the no-js marker, the color-scheme meta,
     the fingerprinted CSS link, the byte-stable inline theme-init script
     (hashed into the CSP by scripts/build-headers.mjs), skip link, header,
     main and footer.

     `class="no-js"` is flipped OFF by the inline theme-init script, which
     always runs when JS is on. That costs no extra bytes (no second script)
     and lets CSS hide JS-only affordances — chiefly the theme toggle, which
     is a dead control with JavaScript off. With no JS the site simply
     follows the OS colour scheme. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="no-js">
<head>
  {% include "partials/head.njk" %}
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ cssManifest.css if cssManifest else '/assets/main.css' }}">
  <script>{{ (themeInit or "") | safe }}</script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  {% include "partials/icons.njk" %}
  {% include "partials/header.njk" %}
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    {% block content %}{% endblock %}
  </main>
  {% include "partials/footer.njk" %}
  <script defer src="/assets/js/theme-toggle.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
